      "Process_Info": {
        "Process_Category": "LPBF + solution annealing + double aging",
        "Process_Text": {
          "original": "The EP-M250 system was employed to fabricate cylindrical blocks measuring 11 cm in height and 1.5 cm in diameter using pre-alloyed GH4169 powder. The manufacturing parameters comprised laser power of 240 W, scanning speed of 980 mm/s, scanning spacing of 0.1 mm and layer thickness of 40 μm. This configuration yielded a volumetric energy density of approximately 61.22 J/mm3. Throughout the manufacturing process, the laser systematically scans the powder layer, inducing melting followed by rapid solidification. After completing a layer, the laser scanning direction is adjusted by 45° to initiate the scanning of the subsequent powder layer. The vertically printed samples were post heat treated. Solution annealing was performed at 980 °C for 1 hour, then cooled with argon gas. This was followed by a first thermal aging stage at 720 °C for 8 hours, cooling in the furnace at 50 °C/h to 620 °C, then a second stage at 620 °C for 8 hours, and finally cooling to room temperature using argon gas.",
          "simplified": "GH4169 cylindrical blocks were fabricated by LPBF on an EP-M250 using 240 W laser power, 980 mm/s scan speed, 0.1 mm scan spacing, 40 μm layer thickness, vertical build, and 45° layer-to-layer scan rotation. The material was then solution annealed at 980 °C for 1 h with argon cooling, followed by double aging at 720 °C for 8 h, furnace cooling at 50 °C/h to 620 °C, then 620 °C for 8 h, and final argon cooling to room temperature."
        },
        "Equipment": "EP-M250",
