      "Microstructure_Info": {
        "Microstructure_Text": {
          "original": "Microstructural characterization of the solution and double-aging post-treated initial material exhibits process-induced imperfections mainly pores, as well as γ′, γ′′ and δ precipitates, carbide, and σ phase. CT characterization showed a porosity of 0.0017% with no obvious lack-of-fusion defects and only a small amount of gas pores. The x-y-z coordinate system was used, where x represents build direction, y longitudinal direction and z transverse direction. XRD on the horizontal y-z plane showed overlapping peaks of γ, γ′ and γ′′. EBSD showed that the longitudinal section contains grains with an average diameter of 17.64 μm, while the transverse section shows grains with an average diameter of 19.36 μm. LPBF GH4169 has weak texture. In the x-y plane, low-angle grain boundaries account for 64.4% and high-angle grain boundaries 35.6%. In the y-z plane, low-angle grain boundaries account for 67.6% and high-angle grain boundaries 32.4%. The average GND density at both x-y and y-z planes is 0.55×10^14/m^2. The observed secondary phases include γ′ with spherical, globular, blocky or cuboidal morphology, γ′′ with disc or plate morphology, δ with needle or plate morphology, MC carbide with globular or blocky morphology, and σ phase with irregular morphology. TEM showed cellular and lamellar substructures in the grains. Circular-like γ′ and needle-like γ′′ precipitates are distributed inside the substructure, δ precipitates are present on the cellular substructure boundary, and NbC/TiC carbides are present near substructure boundaries. For the single-pore fatigue initiation area, the fine grains have an average equivalent diameter of 120 nm, HAGBs account for 63.2%, LAGBs 36.8%, the maximum pole-figure intensity is 4.91, and the GND density is 15.2×10^14/m^2. TEM showed a typical fine grain diameter of approximately 300 nm and parallel twin boundaries inclined about 50 degrees to the loading direction. EDS and SAED showed ordered precipitates inside the fine grains are dissolved and chemical homogenization occurs before grain refinement. Carbides remain incompletely dissolved. For the pores-colony fatigue initiation area, the middle fine-grained region has an average equivalent diameter of 110 nm, the maximum pole-figure intensity is 10.73, the GND density is 23.7×10^14/m^2, and a typical fine grain diameter of about 200 nm in TEM.",
          "simplified": "The post-treated LPBF GH4169 shows very low porosity gas pores, weak texture, grain sizes of about 18-19 μm depending on section, predominantly low-angle grain boundaries, and an average GND density of 0.55×10^14/m^2. The matrix is gamma with γ′, γ′′, δ, MC carbide and σ secondary phases, together with cellular and lamellar substructures. VHCF crack initiation near internal pores is associated with a fine-grained layer, higher local GND density, twin boundaries, dissolution of ordered precipitates, chemical homogenization, and localized continuous dynamic recrystallization."
        },
